from ./Config import Config
from ./componentProperties/typography/font/FontFamily import FontFamily

export anchor Fonts:
    description:
        Every typeface in Emul comes from Google Fonts. Using one fixed source
        means all three outputs draw text with the very same font files.

    families:
        A @{FontFamily} value names Google Fonts families, exactly as Google
        Fonts lists them, such as `Inter` or `"Playfair Display"`. A name with
        spaces is quoted. Generic families, such as `sans-serif`, and fonts
        installed on the computer are not accepted, because they differ from
        machine to machine.

    defaultFamily:
        A component that does not set fontFamily uses `Inter`.

    fallbacks:
        A fontFamily may list more than one family, separated by commas. The
        first family is used for every character it has. A later family is
        used only for characters the earlier ones lack, such as emoji or
        another script. A family like `"Noto Color Emoji"` is a common last
        entry.

    faces:
        Each fontWeight and fontStyle used with a family must exist in that
        family on Google Fonts. A variable family accepts any weight in its
        range. Emul never fakes a bold or italic face by thickening or
        slanting another one, because browsers and Emul would fake it
        differently. A face the first family does not have is an error.
        Fallback families, after the first, only supply characters the first
        lacks, so for them the closest face they have is used instead.

    fetching:
        Fonts are fetched from Google Fonts dynamically, during compilation.
        Emul looks up each family named in the project in Google Fonts'
        catalogue, to check that it exists and has the weights and styles
        used, then downloads the font files for every family, weight and
        style the rendered compositions use. Files are kept in a
        cache, so a project only downloads each one once, and later builds
        work offline. The cache location can be set in @{Config}.

    inEachOutput:
        - html
            The HTML links the Google Fonts stylesheet for exactly the
            families, weights and styles it uses.
        - svg
            Fonts are either embedded in the file or turned into outlines, as
            set by the SVG fonts option. See the SVG output section.
        - png
            Text is always drawn from outlines, so the PNG never depends on
            fonts at all once rendered.

    versions:
        Google Fonts occasionally updates a family. The cache keeps the
        version first downloaded, so a project's output does not change
        unexpectedly; clearing the cache picks up the newer version.
